<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7213"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 12:03 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.ardmoreite.com/stories/080397/news/news08.html" target=_top>http://www.ardmoreite.com/stories/080397/news/news 08.html</a> <BR> <BR>Bestbud <BR> <BR>Good snag. Bouroughs&#39; mention of being introduced to the &#34;invader&#34; after shooting his wife in the forehead, is very much in line with BTK&#39;s &#34;monster&#34;. Notice also, that he says that the only way for him to deal with it is to write. <BR> <BR>BTK isa eclectic assemblage of other prominant people&#39;s traits. This may explain his monster theory...speaking of which... <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html" target=_top>http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html</a> <BR> <BR>I ran across this somewhere. It is mostly about the same stuff you find on any BTK site, however half way through there is a mention of a factor x theory which I have never heard before.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7213-->
<!--Post: 8709--><!--Time: 1109294687-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8709"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 5:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, I must have read this post pretty quickly when it first came up because after rereading it - I have a question for those that seem to be much more in the know about the Blackout than I. <BR> <BR>Who is Pat J. O&#39;Connor or &#34;PJ&#34;? And how old is he or she?  Can this person possibly be the one referenced by BTK  as &#39;PJ&#39; in lieu or in addition to PJ Wyatt?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8709-->
<!--Post: 8742--><!--Time: 1109303187-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8742"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:rwmm@swbell.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hbt - I don&#39;t know about anyone else - but I never realized that Pat&#39;s initials were PJ too! I&#39;ve always been interested in the &#34;beat generation&#34; angle of this story - and my profile states that I think at least one of the victims was connected through The Blackout Tavern. <BR> <BR>I thought I had exhausted my own personal research on this topic - but you&#39;ve brought it back to life. Thanks!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
